cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CE–CPI Household Spending Crosswalk, 2023–2024"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A category-level crosswalk between US household spending (Bureau of Labor
  Statistics Consumer Expenditure Survey, 2024 release) and consumer prices
  (BLS Consumer Price Index, CPI-U twelve-month averages), covering the same
  two calendar years, 2023 and 2024. Each pairing carries a quality label, and
  one pairing (CE Housing against CPI Shelter) is marked NOT COMPARABLE and
  excluded from analysis. Includes a price-adjusted residual per category,
  which is a deflation and not a measure of quantity.
authors:
  - name: "Bromoney"
    website: "https://bromoney.com"
version: "1.1.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - household expenditure
  - consumer price index
  - consumer expenditure survey
  - United States
  - crosswalk
  - price adjustment
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bromoney-US/average-household-expenses"
url: "https://bromoney.com/en/data/ces-cpi-household-spending-crosswalk-2023-2024"
references:
